{"run_id": "20260802T232211-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-6230e686", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many quantities does analysis 2106.14246 report?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2106.14246 reports 12 distinct quantities. These include improvements over previous analyses, normalization factors, and expected improvements from increased luminosity. \n\nFor example, the analysis reports an improvement over the 2016 CMS analysis with a cross-section improvement factor of 6 and a chargino improvement of 200 GeV. It also reports normalization factors for WZ and ZZ processes, and the expected cross-section-limit improvement from increased luminosity alone.\n\nHere are some specific quantities reported:\n\n- Improvement over previous CMS iteration (chargino improvement: 150 GeV, cross-section improvement factor: 2, LSP improvement: 100 GeV)\n- Improvement over 2016 CMS analysis (chargino improvement: 200 GeV, cross-section improvement factor: 6, LSP improvement: 150 GeV)\n- WZ normalization factor \\( r_{WZ} \\): 1.17 ± 0.05\n- ZZ normalization factor \\( r_{ZZ} \\): 1.02 ± 0.1\n- Expected cross-section-limit improvement from increased luminosity alone: 2\n\nThese are just a few examples of the 12 quantities reported in the analysis.\n\nAnswered from the graph.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2106.14246 reports 12 distinct quantities. These include improvements over previous analyses, normalization factors, and expected improvements from increased luminosity. For example, the analysis reports an improvement over the 2016 CMS analysis with a cross-section improvement factor of 6 and a chargino improvement of 200 GeV. It also reports normalization factors for WZ and ZZ processes, and the expected cross-section-limit improvement from increased luminosity alone. Here are some specific quantities reported:\\n\\n- Improvement over previous CMS iteration (chargino improvement: 150 GeV, cross-section improvement factor: 2, LSP improvement: 100 GeV)\\n- Improvement over 2016 CMS analysis (chargino improvement: 200 GeV, cross-section improvement factor: 6, LSP improvement: 150 GeV)\\n- WZ normalization factor \\( r_{WZ} \\): 1.17 ± 0.05\\n- ZZ normalization factor \\( r_{ZZ} \\): 1.02 ± 0.1\\n- Expected cross-section-limit improvement from increased luminosity alone: 2\\n\\nThese are just a few examples of the 12 quantities reported in the analysis.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2106.14246"], "predicate": "result_reports_quantity"}, "rows": 12, "error": null, "seconds": 0.005}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:143d9989c18fdfb48090e99b", "hepkg:evidence:5e32e6cabc5cc69890eee09d", "hepkg:evidence:635e8aa13d4f8936fa91b374", "hepkg:evidence:65a757a062acf1422c719185", "hepkg:evidence:7bef4eda774246d581d0711b", "hepkg:evidence:82312ff62d48d6af43d15e21", "hepkg:evidence:ab674ab3577c334924eb903b", "hepkg:evidence:b97e9ae84d2193dd37b8da29", "hepkg:evidence:c61203e67968b2a534dd50cd", "hepkg:evidence:d5b45061b9f0f67faff3b005", "hepkg:evidence:f4ca8224097ecf677f1a1b86", "hepkg:evidence:ff32973ae2130589e8de1cb1"], "seen_values": ["0.05", "0.1", "0.89", "1", "1.02", "1.1", "1.12", "1.17", "1.26", "10", "100", "15", "150", "2", "200", "2016", "2017", "2018", "2106.14246", "35", "350", "4", "400", "5", "500", "6", "7", "9", "alone", "analysis", "chargino_improvement_gev", "cms", "combined", "conversion", "cross-section", "cross-section-limit", "cross_section_improvement_factor", "data-taking", "dimensionless", "electron", "expected", "factor", "factors", "from", "improvement", "increased", "iteration", "lsp_improvement_gev", "luminosity", "max_factor", "mismeasurement", "none", "normalization", "observ